          "G18A:p0025:b003"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In the future-state model (see Figure 7-2), we see shifts in both the revenue-generating side of the canvas (increased specialization with specific customers, more online and digital presence, targeted value at the lowest possible cost) and the cost side (digital technologies being a key cost driver, a need for new partnerships, plus the global impacts on partnerships and costs). Some areas, such as key activities and sources of revenue, don’t change. Forming a new business model like this is a very people-oriented process, ideally based on good market, product, and cost data, but with leaders reaching alignment on how the business will deliver the most value in the future.",
